\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Would Jesus have the sinner die?
\par Why hangs He then on yonder tree?
\par What means that strange expiring cry?
\par Sinners, He prays for you and me:
\par Forgive them, Father, O forgive!
\par They know not that by Me they live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou loving, all-atoning lamb,
\par Thee-by Thy painful agony,
\par Thy sweat of blood, Thy grief and shame,
\par Thy Cross and passion on the tree,
\par Thy precious death and life-I pray:
\par Take all, take all my sins away!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O let me kiss Thy bleeding feet,
\par And bathe and wash them with my tears!
\par The story of Thy love repeat
\par In every drooping sinner's ears,
\par That all may hear the quickening sound,
\par Since I, even I, have mercy found.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O let Thy love my heart constrain!
\par Thy love for every sinner free,
\par That every fallen soul of man
\par may taste the grace that found out me;
\par That all mankind with me may prove
\par Thy sovereign everlasting love.
\par                                     Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
